STRING(1)              KERNEL STRING FUNCTIONS                 STRING(1)NAME       string - kernel string functionsSYNOPSIS       string ( -- )       (") ( -- string) compilation       " ( -- string) immediate       length ( string -- length)       copy ( string1 -- string2)       = ( string1 string2 -- flag)       + ( string1 string2 -- string1)       print ( string -- )DESCRIPTION       Kernel support for manipulation of null terminated strings.string ( -- )       Vocabulary containing the null-ended string definitions.(") ( -- string) compilation       Compiled run-time action for string literal. Pushes a pointer       to the inline string onto the parameter stack." ( -- string) immediate       String literal compiler. Used in the following form:               " any string"       The string is not bounded by any size (except memory). length ( string -- length)       Returns the length of the string not counting the null       character ending the string.copy ( string1 -- string2)       Returns a instance copy of the parameter string. The copy is        equivalent the the parameter but is allocated to another memory area.= ( string1 string2 -- flag)       Compares the two strings and returns true if they are equal       else false.+ ( string1 string2 -- string1)       Appends "string2" to "string1" and returns the pointer to       "string1". "string1" is assumed to have space for "string2".print ( string -- )       Prints a string on the current output device.SEE ALSO       forth(1)WARNING       Code written using this word set is not directly portable to       other forth environments.BUG       Pointers are not check. Illegal pointer value will result in       a possible error situation.     COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are pres